Disable libkrun's implicit vsock before adding an explicit one.

smolvm 1.13.1 calls krun_add_vsock on the assumption that libkrun no longer
creates a vsock implicitly ("Upstream libkrun no longer creates an implicit
vsock; add explicitly", launcher_dynamic.rs). The libkrun revision smolvm's own
flake pins (98163265) still defaults VsockConfig to Implicit, and its
krun_add_vsock returns -EEXIST unless the config is Disabled, so every boot on
this pin fails with "krun_add_vsock with TSI failed".

That libkrun exports krun_disable_implicit_vsock, which sets the config to
Disabled. smolvm never calls it. This patch loads the symbol optionally and
calls it before each krun_add_vsock, so the sequence works both on the pinned
libkrun and on newer revisions where the symbol is gone and there is no
implicit vsock to disable.

--- a/src/agent/krun.rs
+++ b/src/agent/krun.rs
@@ -45,6 +45,10 @@
     >,
     pub start_enter: unsafe extern "C" fn(u32) -> i32,
     pub add_vsock: unsafe extern "C" fn(u32, u32) -> i32,
+    /// Present on libkrun revisions that still create a vsock implicitly.
+    /// Optional: newer revisions removed both the implicit vsock and this
+    /// symbol, leaving nothing to disable.
+    pub disable_implicit_vsock: Option<unsafe extern "C" fn(u32) -> i32>,
     /// Add a virtio-console device (the upstream replacement for the removed
     /// `krun_set_console_output`). Unix: input/output/err file descriptors.
     pub add_virtio_console_default:
@@ -169,6 +173,7 @@
